# Generated code-graph cache — do not commit.
#
# behavior.json is deliberately NOT listed. Its observed coverage is captured
# by running the test suite, so it cannot be rebuilt by re-reading source the
# way these can — committing it is what gives a fresh clone a blast radius.
#
# graph.*.json is the per-backend artifact (ADR-028): each substrate writes its own,
# so a swap can be diffed instead of destroying the baseline it should be measured
# against. graph.json stays the active graph that other skills read.
#
# docs.json is the doc-section -> code edge set. Parsed from the markdown that is
# already committed, so it is regenerable in the same sense the graph is.
graph.json
graph.*.json
classifications.json
docs.json
